# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Node
node_modules/
web/dist/
.vite/

# Env & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Containers
.lapidary-data/
volumes/

# The default storage root. deploy/compose.yaml binds ${LAPIDARY_STORAGE_ROOT:-../storage}
# into api and worker, and compose resolves that against deploy/, so an operator who sets
# nothing gets the user's own parts library right here, inside the working tree. Never
# ours to commit, and it must not sit in `git status` inviting a broad `git add`. Note
# what an ignore entry cannot do: `git clean -xfd` removes ignored files by definition,
# so a store that matters belongs outside the repository — set LAPIDARY_STORAGE_ROOT.
/storage/

# Generated
sidecar/occt-bridge/build/
crates/*/bindings/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Third-party model archives. A 156 MB .rar was once swept into a docs commit by a broad
# `git add` and made the repository unpushable — GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB.
# Keep such archives outside the repo entirely.
*.rar

# Materialized by `cargo xtask setup` from the marketplaces .claude/settings.json
# declares. A cache of another repository, never a copy this one owns.
/.agents/skills/
/.agents/.cache/

# Transient agent worktrees — a second full checkout of this repository, created and
# removed by tooling. A broad `git add` here commits an entire copy of the tree into
# itself, which is the same accident the .rar rule above records, one order of magnitude
# larger. Never committed, never needed.
/.claude/worktrees/

# The impeccable design detector's engine: a 16 MB platform-specific binary that
# `npx impeccable install` fetches per machine. Its own hooks are written
# `[ ! -f <binary> ] || <binary> hook`, so an absent engine is a no-op rather than a
# broken session — which is what makes leaving it out of the tree safe. The skill, its
# reference material and its hooks are committed; only the compiled linux-x64 artefact
# is not, because a binary in git is forever and this one is wrong on any other arch.
.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/bin/
